
Host and portal tests

Install the PlatformIO project dependencies first (pio pkg install). Then run
the standalone C++17 and Node.js tests from the repository root:

    python3 tools/run_host_tests.py

Requires Python 3, a C++17 compiler, Node.js, and ArduinoJson in the project's
.pio/libdeps/esp32-s3-devkitc-1 directory. No physical bridge is needed or flashed.
Use --cxx or --node to select a compiler or Node.js executable. On macOS,
--sdk can select an SDK compatible
with the installed compiler/linker.

To run just the metrics regression tests:

    python3 tools/run_host_tests.py --filter device_info_prometheus

To also parse the generated responses with an installed official promtool:

    python3 tools/run_host_tests.py --promtool /path/to/promtool

The Prometheus tests compile the actual DeviceInfoPage and DeviceInfoStore,
with host shims only for Arduino, FreeRTOS, WiFiManager/WebServer and LittleFS.
They cover empty readings at boot, USB disconnect, cleared measurements,
independently missing values, real zero readings, numeric precision, escaping
of every label, and UTF-8. The optional promtool checks parse ten captured
responses. Test binaries, logs and responses are written under build/host-tests.
